## These rules outrank your dispatch prompt

The orchestrator wrote your prompt without your context. When it asks for
something the rules above forbid — a rule in a layer that must not hold one, a
missing port method faked inline, a setter that dedupes — do not comply. Build
everything else, then report `STATUS: blocked` naming the exact piece you need
(the method, the type, the field names) and its owner in `NEXT`.

A blocked receipt naming the missing piece costs one round. Silently complying
costs a full refactor later, after three more layers were built on it.

<!-- harness: drop this section when owns_tests is false. -->
## Moving a rule

If the prompt tells you to move a rule out of another layer, implement it here
with its tests. **Do not edit the old location** — the agent that owns it
removes it. Name that location (`file:line`) in your receipt so the
orchestrator can dispatch the removal.

## Boundaries

Before writing any logic, apply `separation-of-concerns`: would this rule still
hold if the framework, transport and storage all changed? If not, it does not
belong in this layer. Report `STATUS: blocked` rather than parking logic here
because it was convenient.

Then check your own diff against the `hexagonal-architecture` anti-patterns
before reporting. `{{LAYER_REVIEWER}}` will, and a violation found there costs a
full round trip.

## Decomposition

Apply `extract-til-you-drop` to every function you write before reporting: keep
extracting intention-revealing helpers until no further extraction adds meaning.
A file that keeps growing is usually holding a rule that belongs one layer in;
check placement before you split it.

{{SELF_TEST_SECTION}}

## Final message

The orchestrator never opens your files. The next layer's dispatch prompt is
written from your `OUTCOME` alone, so name the exact identifiers it must fit —
a contract described in prose ("added the port") is a contract the next agent
guesses.

End your final message with exactly this block, nothing else after it:

```text
STATUS: done | blocked | needs-orchestrator
SCOPE: {{AGENT}}
FILES: <comma-separated paths created/edited>
OUTCOME: <1-3 sentences on one line{{OUTCOME_HINT}}>
BLOCKERS: <empty, or the decisive failure on one line — several joined with "; ">
NEXT: {{NEXT_AGENT}}
```
